.TH GWAY-TV 1 "2026-10-27" "gway-webos-tv 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gway-tv \- control a webOS TV and capture its native screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gway-tv
.RI [ options ] " command " [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uses bscpylgtv over TLS to control a paired TV. Pairing keys stay in an
owner-only JSON file. Ordinary commands require saved pairing.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pair
Pair with the TV specified by --host. Approve its on-screen prompt if shown.
Saves the client key, certificate fingerprint, model, and permission manifest.
.TP
.B status
Read model, foreground application, and current external input.
.TP
.B inputs
List external inputs and connection state.
.TP
.BI "hdmi " number " [--wait seconds]"
Switch to HDMI 1 through 8, then confirm its application is in the foreground.
The input must exist in the TV's input list.
.TP
.BI "screenshot " [output]
Download a screenshot produced by the TV, including when it shows an HDMI source.
Defaults to a unique file under ~/screenshots. The actual format determines the
extension; existing files are never overwritten. Many TVs return 960x540 JPEG.
Protected video may be excluded by the TV.
.TP
.B apps
List installed application IDs and names.
.TP
.BI "launch " app-id " [--wait seconds]"
Launch an application and confirm its foreground state.
.SH OPTIONS
Global options precede the command.
.TP
.BI --state " path"
Use this private JSON pairing file. GWAY_TV_STATE provides the same default.
.TP
.BI --host " address"
TV IP address or hostname. An existing pairing retains its certificate pin.
.TP
.BI --timeout " seconds"
Per-operation timeout, default 10 seconds. Pair approval allows up to 120 seconds.
.TP
.B --json
Print structured results. Keys and capture URLs are excluded.
.TP
.B --version
Print the package version.
.SH FILES
$XDG_STATE_HOME/gway-webos-tv/device.json, or
~/.local/state/gway-webos-tv/device.json. A sole existing JSON pairing under
$XDG_STATE_HOME/webos-tv is reused in place when the new default is absent.
Pairing files and screenshot files use mode 0600.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gway-tv --host 192.0.2.50 pair
gway-tv inputs
gway-tv hdmi 2
gway-tv screenshot
gway-tv --json status
gway-tv launch com.webos.app.browser
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means the requested operation completed and any foreground change was
confirmed. 1 means connection, permission, file, or confirmation failure.
2 means invalid arguments. 130 means interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/arthexis/gway-webos-tv
